  "result": "I reviewed `packet.md` (the `store.py` diff for `last_n`) and wrote `review-payload.json`.\n\n**Finding:** the rewrite from `items[-n:]` to `items[max(0, len(items) - n):]` correctly fixes the stated bug (returning the whole list when `n` exceeds the length), but it silently changes behavior for `n == 0`: `items[-0:]` (old) returns the full list because `-0 == 0` in Python, whereas the new expression computes `items[len(items):]`, an empty list. That's an unannounced behavior change beyond what the PR description claims to fix, so I flagged it as a P2/consider item rather than a blocking defect, since it's plausible (even likely) this is desirable/intended but should be called out explicitly.",
